    },
    {
      "doc_ref" : "6040FD87-97F9-4B8A-B56D-D6450FCD6EB6",
      "object_id" : "24EACEF8-C5F9-4F89-BF23-A2D060E7482D",
      "rect_position" : 15,
      "type_id" : 12
    },
    {
      "direction" : 1,
      "doc_ref" : "6040FD87-97F9-4B8A-B56D-D6450FCD6EB6",
      "object_id" : "25322747-385D-4D3A-BDFA-49443984DB77",
      "type_id" : 9
    },
    {
      "doc_ref" : "6040FD87-97F9-4B8A-B56D-D6450FCD6EB6",
      "head_type" : 9,
      "object_id" : "259D5113-70AC-46AA-B06C-435E3A83D433",
      "position_ref" : "7D1A77FD-5496-4B1B-8D0C-118B2E8EA703",
      "type_id" : 10
    },
    {
      "alignment" : 0,
      "doc_ref" : "6040FD87-97F9-4B8A-B56D-D6450FCD6EB6",
      "object_id" : "25A44D29-ADF4-4CB7-B126-36AB81D09A48",
      "position" : 0,
      "text" : "A1: User launches Bash from PyCharm and activates the virtualenv¹\nA2: User sources environment\nA3: User runs `make claudehook` to register a pre-command hook with Claude Code\nA4: `make claudehook` invokes claudehook.py to modify Claude's local project settings accordingly\nA5: User invokes _select to switch deployments\nA6: _select updates azul_current_deployment in Bash's environment\nA8: _select updates azul_current_deployment in environment.hook\n\nB1: User launches Bash from PyCharm, activates the virtualenv¹ but does not source environment\nB2: User starts Claude Code; inheriting a clean environment\nB3: Claude Code reads the hook configuration from its local project settings\nB4: Before Claude Code runs a Bash command, it invokes claudehook.py\nB5: claudehook.py reads azul_current_deployment from environment.hook and prefixes the command with `azul_current_deployment= ... && source environment`\nB6: Claude launches the processed Bash command; Bash inherits azul_current_deployment and sources the environment²\n\nC1: User starts Python from the virtualenv within PyCharm; this could be an interactive console, a unit test or some script\nC2: envhook.py³ is activated as the virtualenv's site hook\nC3: envhook.py reads azul_current_deployment from environment.hook\nC4: envhook.py loads the environment for the specified deployment\nC5: envhook.py populates the environment of the Python process\n\nD1: User launches Bash from PyCharm; activates virtualenv¹\nD2: User sources environment \nD3: User runs `make claudeunhook` to deregister the pre-command hook from Claude Code⁴\nD4: `make claudeunhook` invokes claudehook.py to modify Claude's local project settings accordingly\nD5: User invokes _select to switch deployments\nD6: _select updates azul_current_deployment in Bash's environment\nD7: _select updates azul_current_deployment in environment.hook\nD8: User starts Claude Code; inheriting an already populated environment\nD9: azul_current_deployment is absent from Claude's local project settings\nD10: Claude Code runs a command; inheriting the already sourced environment⁵\n\n¹ PyCharm's terminal can be configured to automatically activate the virtualenv\n\n² This is the main advantage of using `make claudehook`: Switching deployments,\n  logging in, and changes to the environment*.py files are all effective\n  immediately, without restart, and in all Claude Code instances for the current\n  project (working copy).\n\n³ envhook.py is invoked in every interpreter in the virtualenv but the behavior\n  described here is only activated when the interpreter is directly invoked by\n  PyCharm\n\n⁴ Scenario D is mutually exclusive with scenarios A and B: any attempt by Claude\n  Code to run a command when Claude was launched from a populated environment\n  while claudehook.py is registered will fail with an obvious error.\n\n⁵ Claude will continue to use the deployment that was selected when it was\n  launched. Multiple Claude instances launched this way may use different\n  deployments but any changes to environment*.py or expiring credentials require\n  a restart of Claude and a resumption of the session.\n",
      "type_id" : 27
    },
